    "phrase entropy: first 16 (12 words) or 32 (24 words) bytes of BLAKE3 derive_key(\"Salarium phrase entropy v1\", system ‖ hardware); refused when a source's halves are equal or the sources are equal",
    "device signature: Ed25519 (strict) over the message, or ECDSA P-256 over SHA-256(message) as r ‖ s (32 bytes each, big-endian) with s ≤ n/2; P-256 keys SEC1-compressed (33 bytes)",
    "transaction v3: Borsh {sender, nonce u64, fee u64, valid_until_slot u64, action}; sender tag 0 = Key [u8; 32], tag 1 = Account [u8; 20]; id = BLAKE3 derive_key(\"Salarium transaction v3\", genesis hash ‖ transaction)",
    "action Account is tag 7, an AccountAction: tag 0 AddDevice {key, kind, limit}; 1 RemoveDevice {key}; 2 SetLimit {key, limit}; 3 ReplaceRoot {root_digest [32]}; 4 SetPolicy {policy}; 5 Cancel {id [32]}; 6 SetController {expected_tip [32], controller: ControllerInit}",
    "ControllerInit (23-upgrades §3): tag 0 Managed1 {root_digest [32], devices: Vec of {key, kind, limit}, policy}; one tag per controller version, appended",
    "SetController: expected_tip must equal the account's log tip before the transaction (zeros before the first event); from a kind 0 key (SingleKey) it applies at once; from Managed1 it weakens: a quorum applies it at once, one signer registers it for the delay; once it applies, the old controller's pending actions are gone and the new one starts with that root at index 0, those devices, that policy, the log going on",
    "Controller (an account's stored controller): tag 0 Managed1 {root_digest [32], root_index u32, devices: Vec of {key, kind, limit, spent, day u64, added u64}, policy, pending: Vec of {id [32], action, by: tag 0 Root | tag 1 Device(key), effective u64}, dispute: Option<u64>, log_seq u32, log_tip [32]}",
    "AccountLeaf (23-upgrades §2): tag 0 V1(Account {salt u64, work u64, nonce u64, channels: [Option<{exchange [32], deposit u64, closing_at Option<u64>}>; 2], stake {amount u64, unlock_at Option<u64>}, controller: Option<Controller>, alias: Option<[32]>}); leaf commitment = BLAKE3 derive_key(\"Salarium account v1\", leaf)",
    "device key: tag 0 Ed25519 [32], tag 1 P256 [33]; kind: 0 phone, 1 browser, 2 service, 3 guardian; limit {salt u64, work u64}; policy {delay u64, dispute_timeout u64}",
    "proof: tag 0 Key [64]; 1 Device {index u8, signature [64]}; 2 Devices (two device signatures, increasing index); 3 Root {scheme u8, public_key [32], next_digest [32], signature [64]}; 4 RootAndDevice (root, device); signed = transaction ‖ proof; scheme 0 (Ed25519) is the only one taken",
    "a device signs the transaction id; the root signs root use (id, next_digest) and the account's root digest becomes next_digest",
    "key event: Borsh {account [20], seq u32, prev [32], slot u64, body}; body tag 0 Signed(signed transaction), tag 1 Matured(transaction id [32]); id = BLAKE3 derive_key(\"Salarium key event v1\", event); prev of the first event is 32 zero bytes",
    "from protocol version 2 a quorum's signers sign its quorum message q = BLAKE3 derive_key(\"Salarium quorum v1\", transaction id ‖ [proof tag] ‖ the devices' indexes in the proof's order): Devices (tag 2) two indexes, RootAndDevice (tag 4) one; the devices sign q, the root signs root use (q, next_digest); one signer (Key, Device, Root) signs the id in every version; a log check takes either form of a quorum, the chain held each to its block's version",
    "log check: replay from the origin (root_digest_0 of a kind 5 address, or the key of a kind 0 one) under the chain and the network's account_policy, each event under the controller in force at it; the address's first transaction acts as a quorum's; a quorum's or a strengthening action applies at once, any other account action waits for its Matured event; a SetController that applies voids what was registered before it",
    "from protocol version 3 (protocol::COMPRESSED_P256) a P-256 device key a block takes (AddDevice, SetController's devices) is SEC1-compressed alone, 02 or 03 ‖ x; versions 1 and 2 take the compact form 05 ‖ x too, which names the point of x with the smaller y (a second encoding of half of all keys); a device the chain holds keeps signing in every version; a log check takes the forms every version took (`device_key_forms`)"
